# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the `asan` preset (see ADR-0001 and the
# COE_SANITIZE block in CMakeLists.txt).
#
# Rules: only leaks allocated entirely inside third-party, uninstrumented system
# libraries (Vulkan loader, ICDs, layers, system SDL3) may be listed, one
# `leak:<module or function>` per line, each with a comment saying which test
# hit it, on which driver, and why it is not our bug. Never suppress our own
# code (src/, tools/, engine/, game/).
#
# Earlier noise: the seen so far (2-3 x 128 B one-time Mesa
# allocations reported via "<unknown module>" frames, RADV and lavapipe) came
# from the loader dlclose()ing drivers, and is fixed at the source by
# VK_LOADER_DISABLE_DYNAMIC_LIBRARY_UNLOADING=1 in the test environment.

# smoke_window / input_script_window under asan (window label, so not in the
# standing `ctest -LE window` run; seen on Wayland/KDE, RADV, system SDL3 3.4.18,
# libwayland-client 1.26, step 9): 2 x 96 B calloc'd inside libwayland-client's
# wl_display_read_events during SDL_Init(VIDEO)'s wl_display_roundtrip, i.e.
# wayland event/proxy state owned by the system library, never by our code.
leak:wl_display_read_events
